# The shape the extractor actually produces, with the two spellings from
# issue #48's reproduction: a zero-length insertion into a shared header,
# recorded as './inc/shared.h' by the TU that included "inc/shared.h" and
# as the absolute path by the TU that reached it through -I.
#
# Zero-length insertions never enter the conflict-cluster machinery — they
# go straight to the survivor set — so the ONLY thing that deduplicates them
# is the pre-dedup pass keyed on (file, offset, length, text). That pass
# therefore has to see one canonical file path, or both insertions survive
# and clang-apply-replacements inserts the attribute twice.

# RUN: rm -rf %t.dir
# RUN: mkdir -p %t.dir/inc %t.dir/sub
# RUN: printf '%%80s' '' > %t.dir/inc/shared.h
# RUN: printf '%%80s' '' > %t.dir/a.c
# RUN: printf '%%80s' '' > %t.dir/sub/b.c

# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/single-zero-length-insert.tpl.yaml %t.dir/a.yaml
# RUN: cp %S/Inputs/single-zero-length-insert.tpl.yaml %t.dir/b.yaml
# (One -e per sed: under lit, BSD sed binds -i's suffix to the next word.)
# RUN: sed -i'' -e "s|MainSourceFile:  '@FOO@'|MainSourceFile:  'a.c'|; s|@FOO@|./inc/shared.h|g" %t.dir/a.yaml
# RUN: sed -i'' -e "s|MainSourceFile:  '@FOO@'|MainSourceFile:  'sub/b.c'|; s|@FOO@|%/t.dir/inc/shared.h|g" %t.dir/b.yaml

# RUN: cd %t.dir && clang-ssaf-src-edit-merge -o %t.dir/merged.yaml \
# RUN:     %t.dir/a.yaml %t.dir/b.yaml 2> %t.dir/stderr.txt

# Exactly ONE insertion survives, at the canonical path. The two inputs
# name different main source files, so MainSourceFile is ''. Path literals
# assume a symlink-free %t; see canonical-path-dedup.test.
# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.dir/merged.yaml -DDIR=%/t.dir %s
# CHECK:      MainSourceFile:  ''
# CHECK-NEXT: Replacements:
# CHECK-NEXT:   - FilePath:        '[[DIR]]/inc/shared.h'
# CHECK-NEXT:     Offset:          10
# CHECK-NEXT:     Length:          0
# CHECK-NEXT:     ReplacementText: '.data()'
# CHECK-NEXT: ...
# CHECK-NOT: FilePath:

# RUN: FileCheck --input-file=%t.dir/stderr.txt --allow-empty --check-prefix=NOSTDERR %s
# NOSTDERR-NOT: {{conflict:|does not exist}}
